{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GvxDKvBcenDhe3kWcarxRN","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t## M1: Scala and sbt setup (Status: ✅ DONE)\n41\t\n42\tEstablish the build so `just check` is the one CI gate before any domain\n43\tcode exists.\n44\t\n45\t**Acceptance Criteria:**\n46\t\n47\t- [x] `build.sbt` targets Scala 3 and declares `cats-core`, `cats-effect`, and, in `Test` scope, `munit`, `munit-cats-effect` and `munit-scalacheck`, per `docs/rules/WOW.md`.\n48\t- [x] `sbt compile` succeeds with `-Werror` in `scalacOptions` and zero warnings on a stock scaffold.\n49\t- [x] `sbt test` exits 0 with zero tests collected (no test sources yet).\n50\t- [x] A checked-in `.scalafmt.conf` makes `sbt scalafmtCheckAll` pass.\n51\t- [x] `just check` runs scalafmt-check, compile and test in one invocation and exits 0 on a clean checkout.\n52\t- [x] Sources live under `src/main/scala`, tests under `src/test/scala`.\n53\t- [x] `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (or equivalent) runs `just check` on `push` and `pull_request`, so a red gate locally is red in CI.\n54\t\n55\t**Implementation Details:** `build.sbt` sets `scalaVersion := \"3.3.4\"` (the\n56\tcurrent LTS) and adds `cats-core` 2.12.0, `cats-effect` 3.5.7, and, in\n57\t`Test` scope, `munit` 1.0.3, `munit-cats-effect` 2.0.0 and\n58\t`munit-scalacheck` 1.0.0, matching `docs/rules/WOW.md`. `scalacOptions`\n59\tincludes `-deprecation`, `-feature`, `-unchecked` and `-Werror`.\n60\t`project/plugins.sbt` adds `sbt-scalafmt` 2.5.2 so `sbt scalafmtCheckAll`\n61\tis a real sbt task, and `project/build.properties` pins `sbt.version` to\n62\t1.10.7 (the nix-provided `sbt` binary is a self-updating launcher that\n63\tfetches this version on first run). `.scalafmt.conf` targets the\n64\t`scala3` dialect. `src/main/scala` and `src/test/scala` exist as the\n65\tsource roots but are empty — there is no domain code yet, so `sbt\n66\tcompile` has zero sources/warnings and `sbt test` collects zero tests,\n67\tboth exiting 0. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `just check` on `push`\n68\tand `pull_request` using `actions/setup-java`, `sbt/setup-sbt` and\n69\t`extractions/setup-just`. Verified locally: `just check`, `sbt compile`,\n70\t`sbt test` and `sbt scalafmtCheckAll` all exit 0 with zero warnings and\n71\tzero tests collected.\n72\t\n73\t## M2: Cats hello world (Status: IMPLEMENTED)\n74\t\n75\tProve the Cats Effect edge end to end before any domain logic.\n76\t\n77\t**Acceptance Criteria:**\n78\t\n79\t- [x] The entry point extends `IOApp` (or `IOApp.Simple`) — no `App`, no top-level `main` running side effects directly.\n80\t- [x] `sbt run` prints a greeting to stdout and exits 0.\n81\t- [x] The greeting text comes from a pure function with no `IO` in its signature; a test calls it directly and asserts on the returned string, no I/O involved.\n82\t- [x] A `munit.CatsEffectSuite` test runs the `IO` that prints the greeting and asserts on its result.\n83\t\n84\t**Implementation Details:** `todo.Main` extends `IOApp`; its `run` only\n85\tdelegates to `todo.Cli.run`. `todo.Greeting.message` is the pure greeting\n86\tstring, tested directly with no `IO`. `todo.Cli.greet(out: PrintStream): IO[Unit]`\n87\tis the effectful side — it takes the output stream as an explicit\n88\tparameter rather than writing to `System.out` directly, so the\n89\t`munit.CatsEffectSuite` test in `CliSuite` runs the real `IO`, captures\n90\twhat it printed to a `ByteArrayOutputStream`-backed `PrintStream`, and\n91\tasserts on that, with no mocking and no global state. `Main` calls\n92\t`Cli.greet(System.out)` at the edge. With no arguments, `Cli.run` treats\n93\tthe command as `Command.Greet`, so `sbt run` (no args) prints the\n94\tgreeting and exits 0 — the M3 subcommands (`add`, `list`) are added\n95\talongside it, and any other input reports \"Unknown command\" and exits\n96\tnon-zero.\n97\t\n98\t## M3: Create and read todos (Status: IMPLEMENTED)\n99\t\n100\tThe pure domain model and the YAML-backe